<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian retail sales rise 2.9 pct in May.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian retail sales rise 2.9 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian retail sales rise 2.9 percent to A$10.586 billion in May, seasonally adjusted, after falling 1.7 percent to A$10.285 billion in April, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In May 1996, retail sales rose 0.5 percent to A$10.19 billion.</p>
<p>Analysts median expectations had centred on a rise of around 2.0 percent for May.  </p>
<p>Australian retail sales, May 1997 (A$ billion)</p>
<p>			    May 97  April 97 m/m pct  May 96  y/y pct</p>
<p>    Seasonally adj    10.59    10.29   +2.9     10.19    +3.9</p>
<p>    Unadjusted	  10.50     9.96   +5.5     10.14    +3.6</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates   10.51    10.47   +0.4     10.22    +2.8</p>
<p>Retail turnover by group percentage change, seasonally adj.</p>
<p>				May 97	April 97	May 96</p>
<p>Food retailing	     +3.4	   -3.6	   +1.6</p>
<p>Department stores	  +8.0	   -9.5	   -1.7</p>
<p>Clothing, soft goods     +4.8	   +2.3	   +1.0</p>
<p>Household goods	    +2.8	   -4.2	   +0.6</p>
<p>Recreational goods	 -1.2	   +7.4	   -2.5</p>
<p>Other retailing	    +1.6	   +5.2	   +2.3</p>
<p>Hospitality, services    +0.8	   +1.0	   -0.7</p>
<p>Total			  +2.9	   -1.7	   +0.5</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
